  "response_text": "The PSP\u2019s (Process Stack Pointer) purpose is to tell the CPU where the thread\u2019s stack is located. If we don\u2019t set the PSP before running the thread, then the CPU will try to use the wrong memory location when restoring the registers for that thread. This can cause it to misread or write to the invalid memory causing there to be a hard fault. By using switch/case and the __set_PSP function, we can ensure that CPU has a valid pointer to the stack before starting execution.\\n",
